00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:49.200
This is such a high-level question—I&nbsp;
love it! What is the optimum amount of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:55.240
mushrooms to eat every day? I hear too&nbsp;
much is a waste. Huh, I don't think so;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.240 --> 00:17:00.000
I've certainly never heard that. No, no, eat as&nbsp;
many mushrooms as you want! Oh, speaking of which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:06.000
I just made some pasta sauce and totally forgot my&nbsp;
maitake mushrooms—I'm totally going to add some. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:13.920
did a long Q&amp;A talking about polyphenol oxidases.&nbsp;
Didn't I talk about how much? Don't quote me—go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:19.280
to the video where I actually show the data on&nbsp;
how many seconds it takes—it does not take much.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:24.240
What are my thoughts about the NIH report on&nbsp;
a study saying spermidine can cause stroke?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:35.840
I've never heard of that. Alright, now you got&nbsp;
me. I am typing it into PubMed as we speak...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:40.960
serum spermidine in relation to stroke...&nbsp;
so it's not talking about taking spermidine;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:48.640
it's talking about serum spermidine. But serum&nbsp;
spermidine is linked to lower all-cause mortality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.640 --> 00:17:54.440
which is the most important thing. It is the&nbsp;
most predictive nutrient. Following hundreds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:59.320
of individuals between the ages of 45 and&nbsp;
64, they found 146 components of people's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:06.560
diets, and spermidine was the single most&nbsp;
associated with longevity. So, presumably, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:12.680
would wash out any stroke effect if there even is&nbsp;
a stroke effect. And they're certainly not talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:18.800
about taking it as a supplement, so there’s a&nbsp;
possibility of reverse causation or whatever. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:24.880
that is totally interesting—I'm going to look into&nbsp;
that when I do my spermidine update. But so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:29.520
I would stick to my recommendation because of&nbsp;
all-cause mortality—that's the most important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:34.880
thing. But I will look into it—thank you so&nbsp;
much for letting me know, that's exciting!

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:40.360
How do I explain ApoB and how it compares&nbsp;
to LDL for atherosclerosis risk? So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:49.240
ApoB is a protein that's kind of part of LDL,&nbsp;
but it's also a protein found in other kinds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:59.160
of lipoprotein conglomerates. But LDL continues&nbsp;
to be recommended as the best marker. Testing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:03.160
companies are always trying to come up with fancy&nbsp;
methods to test, but LDL is just so dirt cheap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:08.320
they're not making a lot of money on it.&nbsp;
But it's hard to really beat out LDL for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:09.400 --> 00:19:14.440
predicting survival and cardiovascular&nbsp;
disease risk. I would stick with LDL.

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:22.640
“If someone ate a pure carnivore diet, how long&nbsp;
until they would develop scurvy, the vitamin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:31.120
C deficiency disease?” Well, it depends. If you&nbsp;
ate raw meat—I don't recommend eating raw meat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:36.000
don't recommend eating cooked meat either—but raw&nbsp;
meat has some vitamin C. That's how, you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:50.960
the Inuit could survive on eating whale carcasses&nbsp;
without much plant food during the winter months.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:55.960
How long does it take to develop scurvy? I&nbsp;
have videos about it—I think it just takes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:55.960 --> 00:20:01.920
couple of weeks. In fact, I talk about it in&nbsp;
my fasting video. Anyway, it takes a while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:02.440 --> 00:20:08.000
but scurvy is not the reason why you don't want&nbsp;
to do the carnivore diet. You don't want to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:14.520
the carnivore diet because of the saturated&nbsp;
fat intake, the cholesterol intake, etc.

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:21.240
“If you have elevated liver enzymes, can the liver&nbsp;
heal if you drink non-alcoholic beer and wine?”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:28.440
Well, the reason your liver enzymes are high is&nbsp;
because they've been suffering alcoholic damage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:34.000
from the alcohol. If you stop drinking alcohol,&nbsp;
can your liver heal? Absolutely. Your liver has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:43.088
a remarkable ability to regenerate unless it's&nbsp;
really far along. So yes, stop drinking alcohol.

